Last night and today, I used the spoiler file to generate some statistics
regarding artifacts and other weapons.  Here are the results:

Spoilers hereinafter:


Format:
	The columns of numbers represent, from left to right:

	(1) average damage against small creatures who are non-resistant
	    (general) or singled out (specialzed)
	(2) avg. damage against large cratures in the same categories

	(3) avg. damage against all other small creatures (those who are
	    resistant, in the case of general)
	(4) avg. damage against all other large creatures

"General-Purpose" artifacts:
	These do additional damage to most or all creatures.

Name		 S / L 		 S / L
---------------------------------------
Mjollnir	16 / 15		3.5/2.5
Fire/Frost Brand 9 / 13		4.5/6.5
Excalibur	10 / 12		10 / 12
Stormbringer	11*/10.5*	6.5/ 6   (see below)
Snickersnee	10 / 11		10 / 11
Cleaver		10 / 9		10 / 9
Grimtooth	5.5/5.5		5.5/5.5


Specialized Artifacts:
	These do double damage against one class of monster, normal against
	all others.  Thus, all that matters is the weapon type.

Name		weapon type		 S / L		 S / L
---------------------------------------------------------------
Orcrist		two-handed sword	13 / 21		6.5/10.5
Demonbane	long sword		 9 / 13		4.5/6.5
Giantslayer	<same>			<same>		<same>
Sunsword	<same>			<same>		<same>
Werebane	<same>			<same>		<same>
Dragonbane	broadsword		10 / 9		 5 / 4.5
Trollsbane	morning star		<same>		<same>
Ogresmasher	war hammer		 7 / 5		3.5/2.5
Sting		elven dagger		 6 / 4		 3 / 2


Normal weapons (included for comparison):
	These have no bonus for any type(s) of monsters, naturally.

weapon type		 S / L
-------------------------------
dwarvish mattock	6.5/11.5
two-handed sword	6.5/10.5
katana			5.5/6.5
long sword		4.5/6.5
broadsword		 5 /4.5
war hammer		3.5/2.5
elven dagger		 3 / 2
orcish dagger		 2 / 2


The weapons have been listed in descending order of average damage in the
best case.  An exception is Stormbringer, which does more than just damage.
It is really in a class by itself, and cannot rightly be compared to the other
general-purpose artifacts using average damage as the sole basis of comparison.

It is worth noting that, among ALL the artifacts, Mjollnir has the LOWEST
worst-case damage, except for Sting.  Excalibur has the highest worst-case
average damage.

Also, some numbers are meaningless -- for example, Ogresmasher's average
damage against small singled-out creatures is irrelevant: there are no small
ogres.

With a lawful character, I try to get Mjollnir and Excalibur.  With these two,
there's really no monster that can't be brought down relatively quickly.

Finally, two spoilers not in the latest spoilers file:

	Excalibur is automatically rustproofed.  This is probably due to its
	    aquatic origin.

	Excalibur, when found in a ghost pile, retains its blessed status.

